Passed - re-run on 23 September 2026 on build v26.36.9-a90a3f0, QA branch sv9160, read on the screen. The build moved overnight; this is a newer one than the last run.

Re-tested because the report behind it is now marked QA complete - but the verdict below is what was seen, not what the report says.

All five things this case asks for are on the row. Typed P9160-263 and read the part-sale row:
  1. the number and the customer on the main line - "P9160-263  7 Star Truck Repair";
  2. a status badge - "Approved", in green on a pale green background;
  3. a total price - $168.00. This is what was missing before;
  4. a created date - Sep 17, 2026;
  5. an icon on the left of the row.

One thing worth knowing rather than hiding: six of the twenty part sales returned for P9160 show no money. Every one of them is an Estimate or a Declined, and the product's own answer for those rows carries no total at all - the record genuinely has none stored yet, so there is nothing for the row to show. That is data, not a display fault. A tester who happens to land on an estimate will see no price and should not read that as a failure.

What needs to be done: nothing. This behaviour is correct on this build.

Passed - re-run on 22 September 2026 on build v26.36.8-fa74ea8, QA branch sv9160, read on the screen. This check was Blocked before today because the control it starts by clicking did not exist; it does now, so the check could finally be run.

Searched a term that brings back a work-orders group of more than five, then clicked Show all on that group's heading. All four things the check asks for happened:
  - the search panel stayed open and switched to the Work orders tab - the page behind it did not change and no separate results screen opened;
  - twenty rows were listed, scrolling inside the panel;
  - there is no Show all control inside the scoped tab, and nothing loads further;
  - there is no results banner and the typed word was not handed off to a list page.

Not a claim from the report being marked fixed - every one of the four was read off the screen today.

What needs to be done: nothing. This behaviour is correct on this build.
